<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A library module's manifest. The namespace is declared in build.gradle.kts,
  so there is no package attribute here; there is also nothing to declare,
  because GeckoView brings its own manifest entries through the AAR and this
  module adds no permissions, components or providers of its own.

  Worth stating explicitly, since it is the kind of thing a later change gets
  wrong: NOTHING here may add a permission to the consuming app. The engine
  needs none (it is a library inside the app's own process, not a separate
  one), and a permission that appears here would be merged into the APK's
  manifest without appearing anywhere in :app's source.

  And keep double hyphens out of these comments: XML forbids two hyphens in a
  row inside a comment, and a strict parser rejects the WHOLE FILE for it. This
  manifest shipped once with the prose dash between "none" and "it is a
  library" written that way, and :engine:processDebugManifest died with "Error
  parsing AndroidManifest.xml", which reads like a structural problem and is
  not one. Any dash you want here, write as a single hyphen or restructure the
  sentence.
-->
<manifest />
